comments.text:
Its funny, when I was reading part time parliament paper (paxos) and while learning zig and odin language created a pure paxos library and then the first application for that library was to build a multi-master sqlite. The two approaches I took are very different in case of zig I build zaxonlite (
https://github.com/insanai/zaxonlite
) and have a benchmark on it that includes rqlite. It uses WAL replication as strategy. The second attempt I tried in odin is sqlodin (
https://github.com/insanai/sqlodin
), in this the system does not use WAL but run sql query on each node, as result subset of sql query in sqlite are not supported.
